{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA-2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is our best result at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, showing that multimodal fusion with avgpool aggregation provides a ~2.8% boost over the best RNA-only config (config_002, 0.591). However, we have only tested concat fusion; the effect of weighted fusion is completely untested. Question: config_019 is an exact single-variable ablation of config_018, changing only fusion from concat to weighted. This directly tests whether a learned weighting of modalities outperforms simple concatenation, which is a critical design decision for any multimodal system. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is the cleanest possible A/B comparison against our current best, isolating one variable; (2) fusion strategy is a high-leverage design choice that, if improved, benefits all future multimodal configurations; (3) it is low-risk and immediately actionable — a positive result gives a free upgrade to our best config, while a negative result confirms concat is sufficient and redirects budget toward other axes (RNA encoder, image encoder); (4) under a limited budget, resolving this binary question before exploring higher-dimensional changes (new encoders) avoids confounding multiple untested factors simultaneously."
}

